('172','STI-related Ano-rectal Related Syndromes','6','Problems of the Newborn (Neonate)  .......................................','453','453-454','yy Anal discharge yy Rectal Bleeding yy Pruritus yy Rectal pain, yy Tenesmus yy Constipation','yy Anal ulcers or blisters yy Anal growth yy Tenderness on rectal examination yy Anal discharge or bleeding','yy Acetic acid solution (vinegar) test','Treatment objectives yy To eliminate the warts Non-pharmacological treatment yy Protect normal skin with vaseline (paraffin) while applying Podophyllin yy External genital and perianal warts should be washed thoroughly 1- 4 hours after application of Podophyllin and 6-10 hours after application of Imiquimod. yy Cryotherapy with liquid nitrogen, solid carbon dioxide, or a cryoprobe. Repeat applications every 1-2 weeks yy Electrosurgery yy Surgical removal Pharmacological treatment Evidence Rating: [C] yy Podophyllin 10-25% tincture of benzoin, topical, apply directly to the warts avoiding normal skin tissue. yy Protect normal skin with vaseline (paraffin). Repeat treatment at weekly intervals until complete resolution. Or yy Trichloroacetic Acid (TCA) (80-90%), topical, apply carefully to the warts avoiding normal tissue, followed by powdering of the treated area with talcum powder to remove unreacted acid. Repeat treatment at weekly intervals until complete resolution. Or yy Podophyllotoxin, 0.5%, topical, apply 12 hourly three times a week for 4 weeks Or yy Imiquimod, 5% cream, topical, apply three times a week for 16 weeks. Should be washed 6-10 hours after application. Note 16-3 Do not use TCA during pregnancy and lactation. Do not use Podophyllin or TCA on cervical warts. 172. STI-related Ano-rectal Related Syndromes Causes yy C. Trachomatis yy Herpes Simplex Virus-2 (HSV-2) yy N. Gonorrhoea — STI-related Ano-rectal Related Syndromes — Standard Treatment Guidelines, 7th Edition, 2017 454 yy Treponema pallidum Symptoms yy Anal discharge yy Rectal Bleeding yy Pruritus yy Rectal pain, yy Tenesmus yy Constipation Signs yy Anal ulcers or blisters yy Anal growth yy Tenderness on rectal examination yy Anal discharge or bleeding Treatment Treatment objectives yy To relive pain yy To treat for the major causes simultaneously Non-pharmacological treatment yy Keep lesions dry and clean Pharmacological treatment A. For anorectal discharge, treat for gonorrhea and chlamydia (See sections above) B. For anorectal ulcers or vesicles For 1st episode of vesicular lesions treat for herpes simplex virus yy Aciclovir, 200 mg, 4-6 hourly for 7 days (5 doses per day) Or yy Aciclovir, 400 mg, 8 hourly for 7 days Episodic treatment for recurrent HSV vesicular lesions to be started on first day of appearance of lesions yy Aciclovir, 400 mg, 8 hourly for 5 days Or yy Aciclovir, 800 mg, 12 hourly for 5 days Or yy Aciclovir, 800 mg, 8 hourly for 2 days And C. For Syphilis yy Benzathine Penicillin G, IM, 1.2 MU in each buttock (total dose 2.4 MU) stat. Or yy Procaine Penicillin Aqueous, IM (by deep injection), 1.2 MU daily for 10 days Or',NULL,'— STI-related Ano-rectal Related Syndromes  —
Chapter 16: Sexually Transmitted Infections 
453
Investigations
yy
Acetic acid solution (vinegar) test
Treatment
Treatment objectives
yy
To eliminate the warts
Non-pharmacological treatment
yy
Protect normal skin with vaseline (paraffin) while applying 
Podophyllin
yy
External genital and perianal warts should be washed thoroughly 
1- 4 hours after application of Podophyllin and 6-10 hours after 
application of Imiquimod.
yy
Cryotherapy with liquid nitrogen, solid carbon dioxide, or a 
cryoprobe. Repeat applications every 1-2 weeks
yy
Electrosurgery
yy
Surgical removal
Pharmacological treatment
Evidence Rating: [C]
yy
Podophyllin 10-25% tincture of benzoin, topical, apply directly to the 
warts avoiding normal skin tissue. 
yy
Protect normal skin with vaseline (paraffin). 
Repeat treatment at weekly intervals until complete resolution.
Or
yy
Trichloroacetic Acid (TCA) (80-90%), topical, 
apply carefully to the warts avoiding normal tissue, followed by 
powdering of the treated area with talcum powder to remove unreacted 
acid.
Repeat treatment at weekly intervals until complete resolution.
Or
yy
Podophyllotoxin, 0.5%, topical, apply 12 hourly three times a week 
for 4 weeks  
Or
yy
Imiquimod, 5% cream, topical, apply three times a week for 16 
weeks. Should be washed 6-10 hours after application.
Note 16-3
Do not use TCA during pregnancy and lactation. 
Do not use Podophyllin or TCA on cervical warts.
