d up to a maximum of 300 mg daily for treat­ ment duration Isoniazid and Eth­ ambutol resistant (H-E) Poly-Resistant TB 9 months of R-Z-Lfx Extend treatment to 12 months if extensive lung destruction from x-ray image H, E, and S (±Z) Poly-Resistant TB 3 months of Km-Pto-Lfx-R-Z 15 months of Pto-Lfx-R-Z Modified MDR regimen plus R R mono- or poly- resistance Rifampicin-Re­ sistant TB 8 months of H-Z-Cm-Lfx-Pto- Cs (PAS*) 12 months of H-Z-Lfx-Pto-Cs (PAS*) Full MDR regimen plus H * PAS is alternative to Cs Note 18-6 Definitions Mono-resistant TB: TB bacilli have resistance to only one from the first line anti-tuberculosis medi­ cines: streptomycin, isoniazid, rifampicin, pyrazinamide or ethambutol. Poly-Resistant: TB bacilli have resistance to at least two medicines but not to both isoniazid and rifampicin. Rifampicin-Resistant (RR-TB): TB bacilli have resistance to rifampicin, with or without resistance to other first line anti-tuberculosis medicines. This may be mono, poly, multi or extensively drug resistant TB.',NULL,'— Drug resistant tuberculosis (DR-TB)  —
