Note 18-6
Definitions 
Mono-resistant TB: 
TB bacilli have resistance to only one from the first line anti-tuberculosis medi­
cines: streptomycin, isoniazid, rifampicin, pyrazinamide or ethambutol.
Poly-Resistant: 
TB bacilli have resistance to at least two medicines but not to both isoniazid 
and rifampicin. 
Rifampicin-Resistant (RR-TB): 
TB bacilli have resistance to rifampicin, with or without resistance to other first 
line anti-tuberculosis medicines. This may be mono, poly, multi or extensively 
drug resistant TB.'),
