B.      Treatment in Referral Centre 
Note 18-11
Parenteral antimalarials and follow-on treatment.
The current recommendation is to give parenteral antimalarials in the treat­
ment of severe malaria for a minimum of 24 hours (irrespective of the patient’s 
ability to tolerate oral medication) until the patient is able to tolerate oral med­
ication as follow-on treatment. Recommended follow-on treatments include 
ACTs and Quinine + clindamycin. 
