should be delayed and started one week after SP administration. For additional 
information on IPTp and malaria in pregnancy, refer to the latest Ghana Health 
Service training manuals and guidelines on the subject.
190.	Seasonal Malaria Chemoprevention (SMC)
This is the intermittent administration of full treatment courses 
using the recommended anti-malarial medicine during peak malaria 
transmission seasons to prevent malaria illness. A complete treatment 
course is given to children aged between 3 and 59 months at monthly 
intervals to a maximum of 4 doses during the malaria transmission 
season. In Ghana, SMC has been implemented in the Northern Savannah 
using Sulphadoxine-Pyrimethamine and Amodiaquine (SP + AQ)

