191.	Meningitis
This is an infection of the coverings of the brain, and is most 
commonly caused by bacteria, viruses, fungi and protozoa. One type, 
Cerebrospinal Meningitis (CSM), caused by Neisseria meningitides, is 
common in the Northern and Upper Regions of Ghana, and usually 
occurs in epidemics during the harmattan season. The presentation may 
sometimes be confused with cerebral malaria. Meningitis is a medical 
emergency. Failure to recognise and adequately manage meningitis 
results in serious complications.
Inform regional or district health authorities immediately in epidemic 
meningitis.
Causes 
