Referral Criteria 
Refer patients with corneal foreign bodies, intraocular foreign 
bodies, persistent pain and redness of the eye to the eye specialist.
196.	Red Eye
Red eyes are either the result of inflammation of ocular tissue or 
bleeding into the sub conjunctival space. The pattern of the redness, 
nature of the discharge, associated pain and its intensity, vision loss and 
appearance of the cornea are helpful in characterising the red eye.  Red 
eye is a potentially very serious condition especially in situations where 
the redness is around the cornea. 
