time
 
2nd Line Treatment
Evidence Rating: [C]
yy
Polyvinyl alcohol, 1.4-2% eye drops, 1-2 hourly during waking time 
And  
yy
Chloramphenicol, 1% eye ointment, at night before bedtime
Or
yy
Tetracycline, 1% eye ointment, at bedtime
Referral Criteria 
Refer patients whose exposure keratopathy is not improving to the 
eye specialist.
200.	Strabismus
Strabismus is misalignment usually of one eye preventing 
simultaneous viewing of an object by both eyes. Onset in children under 
7 years interferes with the development of the visual system of the 
deviating eye in the brain leading to amblyopia. Acute onset at an older 
age causes double vision. Diplopia does not occur in children because of 
the ability to suppress the second image or development of amblyopia. 
Amblyopia does not occur if the deviation alternated from one eye to the 
other. The more frequent types are horizontal misalignment. Esotropia is 
convergent deviation and exotropia is divergent deviation. 
Causes 
yy
Congenital misalignment
yy
Acquired deviation 
yy
Paralysis of the cranial nerve VI, III or IV'),
