('211','Dental Caries','6','Problems of the Newborn (Neonate)  .......................................','534','534-534','yy Usually asymptomatic yy Toothache precipitated by hot, cold or sweet foods or drinks yy Pain may be intermittent or severe, sharp and constant if the nerve endings are exposed','yy A hole or black spot may be visible on any surface of a tooth yy Tenderness on percussion of the affected tooth',NULL,'Treatment objectives yy To relieve pain yy To arrest process by excavation and filling of cavities yy To educate on good dental habits yy To prevent complications Non-pharmacological treatment yy Regular mouth rinse after refined carbohydrate intake yy Brushing of teeth before bedtime Pharmacological treatment A. For pain relief Evidence Rating: [C] yy Paracetamol, oral,',NULL,'21
Chapter
534
Oral and Dental Conditions 
211.	Dental Caries 
Dental caries is a tooth surface cavity caused by acid demineralization 
of tooth hard tissue. It occurs as a result bacterial conversion of refined 
carbohydrates to acids, which in prolonged contact with tooth surface 
leads to the demineralisation. This process is entirely preventable but can 
progress to severe decay and tooth loss or complicated by infection.
Causes
yy
Acid demineralisation of hard tooth surface
Symptoms
yy
Usually asymptomatic
yy
Toothache precipitated by hot, cold or sweet foods or drinks
yy
Pain may be intermittent or severe, sharp and constant if the nerve 
endings are exposed
Signs
yy
A hole or black spot may be visible on any surface of a tooth
yy
Tenderness on percussion of the affected tooth
Treatment
Treatment objectives
yy
To relieve pain
yy
To arrest process by excavation and filling of cavities
yy
To educate on good dental habits
yy
To prevent complications
Non-pharmacological treatment
yy
Regular mouth rinse after refined carbohydrate intake
yy
Brushing of teeth before bedtime
Pharmacological treatment
A.     For pain relief
Evidence Rating: [C]
yy
Paracetamol, oral,'),
