222.	Trigerminal Neuralgia  
Trigerminal neuralgia is a condition characterised by unilateral facial 
pain that follows the distribution of the trigerminal nerve. It presents with 
recurrent, sudden onset sharp-shooting pain in the face and may have 
a trigger-point.  The patient may present with marked anxiety and may 
mimic a psychiatric disorder.
