224.	Rheumatoid arthritis
Rheumatoid arthritis (RA) is a chronic systemic inflammatory disease 
of unknown cause. An external trigger (e.g. cigarette smoking, infection, or 
trauma) triggers an autoimmune reaction, leading to synovial hypertrophy 
and chronic joint inflammation along with the prospect for extra-articular 
manifestations. It is believed to occur in genetically susceptible individuals 
and more common in middle aged women. 
Causes 
